hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1718","Waki narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam as-Saluli, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan ibn Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me words to say in the qunut of witr: O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, and grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, and take me as ally among those You have taken as ally, and bless for me what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed he whom You befriend is not humiliated. Blessed are You, our Lord, and Exalted."
"1719","Waki narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah: al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us and said: A man parted from you yesterday whom the first ones did not precede in knowledge, nor will the later ones reach him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to send him with the banner, Jibril on his right and Mikail on his left; he would not turn back until victory was granted to him."
"1720","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Hubshi who said: al-Hasan ibn Ali addressed us after the killing of Ali and said: A man parted from you yesterday whom the first ones did not precede in knowledge, nor did the later ones reach him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would send him and give him the banner, and he would not turn back until victory was granted to him. And he left neither gold nor silver except seven hundred dirhams of his stipend which he was setting aside for a servant for his family."
"1721","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Hasan ibn Ali that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught him to say in witr, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Yunus."
"1722","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from al-Hasan ibn Ali that a funeral passed by them and the people stood but he did not stand. al-Hasan said: What have you done? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only stood out of annoyance at the odor of the Jew."
"1723","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, from Abu al-Hawra as-Sadi who said: I said to al-Hasan ibn Ali: What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I remember that I took a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pulled it out with its saliva and threw it among the dates. A man said to him: What is it to you if he ate this date? He said: Indeed we do not eat charity. He said: And he used to say: Leave what puts you in doubt for what does not put you in doubt, for truthfulness is tranquility and lying is doubt. He said: And he used to teach us this supplication: O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, take me as ally among those You have taken as ally, bless for me what You have given, protect me from the evil of what You have decreed; indeed he whom You befriend is not humiliated; and perhaps he said: Blessed are You, our Lord, and Exalted."
"1724","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Thabit ibn Umarah narrated to us, Rabiah ibn Shayban narrated to us that he said to al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: He brought me into the charity room and I took a date from it and put it in my mouth, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Throw it, for it is not lawful for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor for anyone of his household, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1725","Abu Ahmad, he is az-Zubayri, narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Salih narrated to us, Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Abu al-Hawra who said: We were with Hasan ibn Ali and he was asked: What did you comprehend from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I was walking with him and he passed by a store of charity dates, and I took a date and put it in my mouth, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, inserted his finger in my mouth and took it out with my saliva. Some of the people said: What is it to you if you had left it? He said: Indeed we, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us. He said: And I comprehended from him the five prayers."
"1726","Affan narrated to us, Yazid meaning Ibn Ibrahim, and he is at-Tustari, narrated to us, Muhammad informed us, he said: I was informed that a funeral passed by al-Hasan ibn Ali and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both. al-Hasan stood and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, remained seated. al-Hasan said to Ibn Abbas: Did you not see the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a funeral passed by him and he stood? Ibn Abbas said: Yes, and he also sat. al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with them both, did not deny what Ibn Abbas said."
"1727","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrating from Abu al-Hawra, he said: I said to al-Hasan ibn Ali: What do you remember from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I remember from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that I took a date from the dates of charity and put it in my mouth. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, removed it with its saliva and put it among the dates. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what was it to you regarding this date for this boy? He said: Indeed we, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us. He said: And he used to say: Leave what puts you in doubt for what does not put you in doubt, for truthfulness is tranquility and lying is doubt. He said: And he used to teach us this supplication: O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, take me as ally among those You have taken as ally, bless for me what You have given, protect me from the evil of what You have decreed; You decree and none decrees upon You; indeed he whom You befriend is not humiliated. Shubah said: And I think he also said this: Blessed are You, our Lord, and Exalted. Shubah said: One who heard this from him narrated to me, then I heard him narrate this hadith on his way to al-Mahdi after the death of his father, and he did not doubt regarding Blessed and Exalted. I said to Shubah: You doubt regarding it? He said: There is no doubt in it."
"1728","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin that Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan ibn Ali were passed by a funeral; one of them stood and the other sat. The one who stood said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood? He said: Yes, and he sat."
"1729","Abdul-Wahhab ath-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad that al-Hasan ibn Ali and Ibn Abbas saw a funeral; one of them stood and the other sat. The one who stood said: Did not the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stand? And the one who sat said: Yes, and he sat."
